# Disk scheduling

Only matters for spinning disks where seek time dominates; SSDs mostly use noop/none or mq-deadline.

Queue: 98, 183, 37, 122, 14, 124, 65, 67; head at 53; cylinders 0–199.

| Algorithm | Order | Total head movement |
|---|---|---|
| FCFS | as given | 640 |
| SSTF | 65, 67, 37, 14, 98, 122, 124, 183 | 236 |
| SCAN (towards 0) | 37, 14, 0, 65, 67, 98, 122, 124, 183 | 236 |
| C-SCAN (towards 199) | 65, 67, 98, 122, 124, 183, 199, 0, 14, 37 | 382 incl. return |
| LOOK | like SCAN but turns at the last request | 208 (towards 0 first) |
| C-LOOK | like C-SCAN but jumps from the last to the first request | 322 |

SSTF can starve far requests. SCAN is the elevator. C-SCAN gives more uniform waiting times.

Check whether the exam counts the return sweep of C-SCAN as movement; the textbook does, the TA said either is fine if stated.
